{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The frames-and-context family F1 concerns bounded engagement: frame declaration, sizing, binding, activation, relations, coverage and revision. The reference-frame-evaluation member owns engagement under urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation; ACTIVATION owns context construction and FOUNDATIONS owns the referenced frame objects, authority kinds, independence distinctions and frame tuple.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":133,
          "quote":"decides how a finite actor engages a body of work through bounded reference\nframes: how a frame is declared, sized, bound, activated, related to other\nframes, used to audit coverage and revised.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":127
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_context",
      "label":"Frames and context"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Instance premises describe the governed work rather than commitments derivable from finite capacity alone."
      ],
      "definition":"The foundation-to-law table traces consequences, stating rules, added choices, owners, pillars and consumers; it owns none of the named rules. Its instance premises are workspace excess over one actor's competence, context, tools and access; declared questions about a governed outcome; potentially overlapping frames and actors; changes between activations; and access to owning sources and copied, projected or compressed surfaces. P0 is recovered, including actor change without private-memory transfer and an open world; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 are cited as independent; P4b is derived from P0 and P2 with non-reacquirable step-produced facts, and P5 from P0 and P6 with the open-world premise.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":147,
          "quote":"They are conditions of the work this family governs, not\ncommitments, and do not follow from finite capacity alone.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":143
        }
      ],
      "key":"foundation_trace",
      "label":"Foundation-to-law trace"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A reference frame is a finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations required by one evaluation family. It is an engagement unit activated and evaluated as one bounded context, distinct from selection, activation, evaluation, conjunction, translation, coverage and revision functions. Its relation is not a required schema or runtime carrier; a prompt, context packet or program projects an activated frame rather than being the frame. The referenced tuple has twelve components ⟨Q, B, M, C, I, A, E, X, R, J, K, D⟩.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":157,
          "quote":"a reference frame is a finite specification of the attention, coordinates, authority, evidence and result relations one evaluation family requires.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F1.%20The%20frame%20as%20the%20engagement%20unit%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":157
        }
      ],
      "key":"reference_frame",
      "label":"Reference frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The declared family of questions supported by a frame, against which its sufficiency and an evaluation's inclusion are tested at the declared coordinates.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":284,
          "quote":"Every frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no\ndeclared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-001%20Evaluation%20relativity",
          "start_line":283
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_family",
      "label":"Evaluation family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"The selected actor's declared capability boundary, including competence, context capacity, access and tools. Fitting the envelope and adequately attending during actual use are separate questions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":299,
          "quote":"Whether the actor attends adequately to a frame that fits is a separate\nquestion, answered by actual-use evidence under\n[EVALUATION §7](EVALUATION.md#frame-qualification); a size measurement\ndoes not answer it",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-002%20Finite%20attention",
          "start_line":296
        }
      ],
      "key":"capability_envelope",
      "label":"Capability envelope"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Distinguishable roles for semantic law, observational evidence, evaluator application, the existing owner's operation grant where material, and disposing decision authority. Frame-set authority is human authority; actor identity is separate. Acceptance and publication authorities appear separately in the supplied declarations.",
      "exceptions": [
        "One actor may lawfully perform several roles without collapsing them."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":344,
          "quote":"a frame declaration keeps these roles distinguishable even when\none actor lawfully performs several of them, and where the evaluation\nperforms a material operation, the existing operation owner supplies the\nexact grant as a further role the declaration keeps apart",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-007%20Semantic%2C%20evidence%20and%20verdict%20separation",
          "start_line":341
        }
      ],
      "key":"authority_roles",
      "label":"Authority and evaluation roles"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "An evaluation is performed."
      ],
      "definition":"One closed result in the frame's declared algebra: the FOUNDATIONS §4 core or a refinement mapped into it. The named core values are satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis; the frame member applies rather than defines their meanings.",
      "exceptions": [
        "An evaluation not performed has no evaluation result; its stop state belongs to ACTIVATION §3."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":403,
          "quote":"Every performed evaluation of a frame returns one closed result in the\nframe's declared result algebra: the core algebra of\n[FOUNDATIONS §4 Results](FOUNDATIONS.md#results), or a refinement mapped\ninto it under that section.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FRF-012%20Closed%20results",
          "start_line":398
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_result",
      "label":"Closed frame evaluation result"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A domain's unit of semantic irreducibility, distinct from a bounded engagement unit. One frame may contain several semantic atoms and an atom may participate in several frames. Any adopting method's semantic-contraction law governs its own domain atom family.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":467,
          "quote":"Semantic irreducibility is a\nseparate question: one frame may contain several semantic atoms, and one\nsemantic atom may take part in several frames",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F3.%20Laws%2FEngagement%20atom%20and%20semantic%20atom",
          "start_line":463
        }
      ],
      "key":"semantic_atom",
      "label":"Semantic atom"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"A human-declared project selection of frames for a governed workspace and outcome. Its declaration includes known evaluations, envelopes, intentional overlaps, separately activated checks, dependencies or translations, authorities, exclusions, uncertainty and revision conditions. It need not be a partition, tree, stack or exhaustive ontology.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":480,
          "quote":"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated\ndevelopment practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the governed\noutcome's risk and knowledge of the available agents and other actors.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F4.%20Frame-set%20declaration",
          "start_line":476
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_set",
      "label":"Project frame set"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Seven relations distinct from the frame: declare(human_authority, workspace, outcome, practices, capabilities) → frame_set; activate(frame, evaluation, subject, basis, actor) → activated_frame or activation_refusal; evaluate(activated_frame, admissible_evidence) → result, evidence and residuals; conjoin(decision_rule, frame_results) → decision, conflict or indeterminate; translate(source_frame, target_frame, value_or_evidence, mapping) → translated_value, declared_loss or refusal; audit_coverage(workspace, outcome, evaluation_inventory, frame_set) → coverage_ledger; revise(frame_set, new_evidence, failures, capability_change, topology_change) → proposed_frame_set_delta. The displayed signatures are supplemented by expressly stated direct out_of_frame and invalid_basis outcomes. Declaration belongs to §4, activation/evaluation to ACTIVATION §§1–2, return/reuse to ACTIVATION §7, conjunction/translation to §6, audit to §8 and revision to §10; EVALUATION §7 qualifies each.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":530,
          "quote":"The frame and the functions over it remain distinct. An application may\nrealise the following relations in any conforming form; the signatures\ndescribe relations, not callable software interfaces",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F5.%20Method%20functions",
          "start_line":527
        }
      ],
      "key":"method_functions",
      "label":"Frame method relations"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Each evaluation is separately activated and returns its own closed result."
      ],
      "definition":"Several frames evaluate the same subject, potentially sharing subject, manifold or evidence sources, while neither consumes nor influences the other's unclosed working result. This serves assurance independence, different evidence altitudes and distinct failure perspectives without itself establishing every assurance-independence condition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":623,
          "quote":"Several frames may evaluate the same subject through separate activations\nand return closed results. They may overlap in subject, manifold or\nevidence sources; neither evaluation consumes or influences the other's\nunclosed working result.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FIndependently%20activated%20co-evaluation",
          "start_line":618
        }
      ],
      "key":"co_evaluation",
      "label":"Independently activated co-evaluation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "A declared decision rule consumes closed results."
      ],
      "definition":"A relation combining several frames' closed results under FOUNDATIONS §4 Conjunction of results and its core algebra. This member defines no independent conjunction law; §5 defines its outcome refinements.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":632,
          "quote":"A declared decision rule consumes the closed results of several frames.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FResult%20conjunction",
          "start_line":627
        }
      ],
      "key":"result_conjunction",
      "label":"Result conjunction"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another."
      ],
      "definition":"A declared transfer specifying source and target coordinates, preserved meaning, accepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions. ACTIVATION §4 Refinement owns what preservation and loss must show and the licensing law; representation in a_c records preservation, introduced, removed and residual fields under AC-013. This section adds the frame-specific coordinates, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":639,
          "quote":"One frame supplies evidence or a value consumed inside another. The\ntranslation declares source and target coordinates, preserved meaning,\naccepted loss, provenance, equality law and refusal conditions",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FEvidence%20or%20coordinate%20translation",
          "start_line":636
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_translation",
      "label":"Evidence or coordinate translation"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "The evaluation requires the composition."
      ],
      "definition":"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning relation. Its owning application declares the composition, shared invariants, effect or decision order where material, closure, failure and conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority.",
      "exceptions": [
        "A possible future interaction alone does not require a general composition law in every frame."
      ],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":657,
          "quote":"Several frame-governed operations form one material execution or reasoning\nrelation. The owning application declares the composition, the shared\ninvariants, the effect or decision order where material, closure, failure,\nand the conservation of semantic, operation and decision authority.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F6.%20Frames%20in%20conjunction%2FMaterial%20composition",
          "start_line":651
        }
      ],
      "key":"material_composition",
      "label":"Material composition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "A project declares only relations needed by its evaluations and coverage claims."
      ],
      "definition":"Ten named possibilities: disjoint means no material variable, coordinate, evidence or result dependency shared for declared evaluations; overlapping shares some material variables, evidence or entities; complementary evaluations jointly inform one decision; alternative frames evaluate the same claim under declared capability or evidence conditions; refinement resolves another frame's aggregated material distinction; restriction evaluates a lawful subset of another's domain; translated moves values or evidence through a declared coordinate map; temporally successive evaluates a changed basis later; composed forms one governed evaluation or action; governing/subordinate inherits declared constraints where a real authority or decomposition relation exists. None is the universal default topology.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":682,
          "quote":"No relation is the default universal frame topology. A project declares\nonly the relations its evaluations and coverage claims need",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F7.%20Frame%20relations",
          "start_line":680
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_relation_kinds",
      "label":"Declared frame relation kinds"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T) binds workspace W, governed outcome G, exact basis B, known evaluation inventory E, declared frame set S and the claim's time or immutable checkpoint T.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":691,
          "quote":"Coverage is evaluated against the tuple Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): the\nworkspace W, the governed outcome G, the exact basis B, the known\nevaluation inventory E, the declared frame set S and the time or immutable\ncheckpoint T of the claim.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20basis",
          "start_line":688
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_basis",
      "label":"Exact coverage tuple"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Sources are available and material; listed source categories apply where applicable."
      ],
      "definition":"Known evaluations derived by the coverage evaluator from every material available source, recording provenance and materiality. Sources include goals, intent, product definition, requirements, accepted method; accepted design and its ontology, identities, lifecycles, authorities and algorithms; implementation capabilities and observable behaviour; operational, release, security, safety and governance obligations; direct/indirect dependencies and seams; evidence, tests, scenarios, qualification and acceptance claims; tickets, check-ins, commentary, post-mortems, incidents and rejected candidates; long loops, resets, repeated repairs and rival paths; actor capability limits and invisible violations; applicable external law, contracts and standards.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":701,
          "quote":"The coverage evaluator derives the known evaluation inventory from every\nmaterial available source, including where applicable:",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FEvaluation%20inventory",
          "start_line":699
        }
      ],
      "key":"evaluation_inventory",
      "label":"Known evaluation inventory"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "A lens becomes a frame only when separately instantiated as a bounded evaluation family."
      ],
      "definition":"Cross-cutting audit lenses, typically outcome/capability, identity/authority, lifecycle/temporal behaviour, topology/seams, transport/representation, evidence/proof, change/failure/recovery/rollback, historical regression, and actor capability/context fit.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":724,
          "quote":"These are lenses (FOUNDATIONS §2): they become frames only when separately\ninstantiated as bounded evaluation families",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20dimensions",
          "start_line":722
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_lenses",
      "label":"Coverage dimensions"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Audit record containing at least, per evaluation: exact predicate; provenance establishing materiality; exact subject and basis; capable selected frames; required competence/context envelope; semantic owner; existing operation-owner grant for construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation where performed, otherwise none; decision owner; required observations and provenance; material frame/seam dependencies; coverage status; and uncertainty, exclusion or re-entry residual. Statuses describe the row's coverage obligation on its exact tuple, not the evaluated claim.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":729,
          "quote":"The ledger holds at least, for each evaluation",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F8.%20Workspace%20coverage%2FCoverage%20ledger",
          "start_line":728
        }
      ],
      "key":"coverage_ledger",
      "label":"Coverage ledger"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Diagnosis triggered by repeated inability of a competent actor to see known material violations; repairs creating or duplicating authority paths; repeated resets after apparently valid completion; long loops without stable closure; passing proof with an unbound outcome; failures visible only after broad integration; repeated context expansion without a decidable question; actors sharing a frame name but evaluating different material relations; or topology mutation leaving prior verdicts apparently current. Diagnosis itself grants no repair authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":866,
          "quote":"These observations trigger frame diagnosis",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F10.%20Discovery%20and%20revision%2FMissing-frame%20signals",
          "start_line":865
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_diagnosis",
      "label":"Frame diagnosis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Minimum actor packet: frame identity/revision; evaluation/result algebra; exact subject/basis; material relations/invariants; semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authority; admissible evidence/tools; capability/context envelope; exclusions/prohibited assumptions; declared dependencies or conjunction outputs; invalidation, stop and reconfiguration conditions. It presents one activated frame or one declared active frame configuration.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":970,
          "quote":"An actor receives one activated frame or one declared active frame\nconfiguration, never an implied demand to reconstruct the complete\nworkspace from ambient context",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet",
          "start_line":967
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_packet",
      "label":"Activation packet"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Every field resolves through stable identities and source references."
      ],
      "definition":"Carrier-neutral template sufficient to bind one declared frame for one evaluation: stable activation identity; declaration identity/revision; exact evaluation/closed algebra; exact subject or candidate; workspace, authority, dependency, configuration and time basis; material relations/invariants; exact source/semantic references; exclusions/prohibited assumptions; actor/envelope; semantic/evaluation authority; material operation authority, subject and territory; decision/acceptance/publication authority; admissible evidence/acquisition route; used dependency, overlap, input, conjunction or translation relations; expected consumer/return relation; invalidation; stop, residual, re-entry and reconfiguration conditions. The template is descriptive content, not a filled activation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":997,
          "quote":"The following carrier-neutral content is sufficient to bind one declared\nframe for one evaluation. It may be written in Markdown, structured data, a\nprompt or another consumer-selected carrier without changing the relation",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F11.%20The%20activation%20packet%2FMinimal%20activation%20binding",
          "start_line":994
        }
      ],
      "key":"activation_binding",
      "label":"Minimal activation binding template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Three carrier-neutral document shapes described as the least content for a frame, a frame set and an evaluation result, sufficient in Markdown or another consumer-selected carrier.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1076,
          "quote":"The three carrier-neutral shapes below are the least content that declares\na frame, a frame set and an evaluation result. Each is sufficient as\nwritten in Markdown or any other consumer-selected carrier",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations",
          "start_line":1073
        }
      ],
      "key":"minimal_declarations",
      "label":"Minimal declaration shapes"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [
        "Optional frame relations record inputs, outputs, overlaps, conjunctions or translations actually used."
      ],
      "definition":"Frame template with stable local identity; evaluation questions, predicates and closed algebra; workspace boundary, exact identity and version/time/topology coordinates; entities, variables, relations, states and interactions; coordinate distinction/equality; governing invariants; frame-set, semantic, evaluation, material operation and decision authorities; admissible evidence/provenance/exclusions; competence, context, access, tools, evaluation/assurance independence and configuration; irrelevant material, prohibited assumptions and out-of-frame conditions; optional used relations; invalidation/recharting changes; representative qualification cases, counterexamples and residuals.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1089,
          "quote":"# Frame: <stable local identity>\n\n## Evaluation Family\n<questions, predicates, and closed result algebra>",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame%20declaration",
          "start_line":1083
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_declaration_template",
      "label":"Minimal frame declaration template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Frame-set template with stable local identity; workspace, outcome, basis and time; human declaration/acceptance authority; known evaluations/provenance; selected identities/revisions/envelopes; coverage mapping to capable frames; intentional separately activated checks, assurance independence or alternative fit; only evaluation-required conjunction/translation relations; uncovered, unknown, conditional or excluded evaluations; and history, topology, capability, evidence or outcome revision triggers.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1136,
          "quote":"# Frame Set: <stable local identity>",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/claude/c2cfa9b908d1722ae3f26c32fa4ece691083bdc3/source/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md#REFERENCE_FRAME%2F13.%20Minimal%20declarations%2FMinimal%20frame-set%20declaration",
          "start_line":1127
        }
      ],
      "key":"frame_set_template",
      "label":"Minimal frame-set declaration template"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition":"Evaluation-result template with frame identity/revision, activation identity, evaluation, subject/basis, actor/envelope, semantic/evaluation/material operation/decision authority, admissible evidence, result, inference relation, residual uncertainty, out_of_frame residual, invalidation conditions and consuming decision or conjunction.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1176,
          "quote":"- result:\n- inference relation:\n- residual uncertainty:\n- out_of_frame residual (missing relation or capability, owner, reconfiguration pressure):\n- invalidation conditions:\n- consuming decision or conjunction:",
