      "key":"coverage_status_refinement",
      "statement":"The row predicate is capable coverage on the tuple without unresolved frame/result/authority conflict, or a cited governing exclusion. covered maps to satisfied when a capable selected frame evaluates it without unresolved conflict; separately_covered maps to satisfied when separately activated selected frames each evaluate it without unresolved conflict; excluded_by_authority maps to satisfied for the cited governing exclusion. conditionally_covered maps to indeterminate, naming the unestablished condition and deciding evidence. conflicted maps to falsified, retaining unresolved conflict as counterexample for decision authority. uncovered maps to falsified when no capable selected frame evaluates it and no cited authority excludes it, with absence as counterexample. unknown maps to indeterminate when admissible evidence cannot decide coverage, including unknown capability or materiality. Each core value travels with the coverage predicate and status. None is a result of the covered evaluation. Exclusion meets the obligation without performing or covering the evaluation. In conjunction of the governed claim an uncovered row is unaddressed required coverage, never a falsified component. Conditional, conflicted, unknown and uncovered statuses are never read as covered, nor exclusion as failure.",
